{"name":"Pompeian Red","hex":"#a82a38","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pompeian red","blocks":[{"text":"Pompeian red refers to the color of iron oxide-based mineral pigment with a hue close to red ochre, so named because of its common use in ancient Roman painting and the fact that it is abundant in the murals of Pompeii. Studies have shown that walls with Pompeian red backgrounds were painted in various ways, of which the use of cinnabar was the most expensive."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pompeian_red"},{"title":"Pompey","blocks":[{"text":"Gnaeus Pompeius Magnus, known in English as Pompey or Pompey the Great, was a Roman general and statesman who was prominent in the final decades of the Roman Republic. As a young man, he was a partisan and protégé of the dictator Sulla, after whose death he achieved significant military and political success."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/%28Venice%29_Pompey_the_Great%2C_Museo_Archeologico_Nazionale.jpg/330px-%28Venice%29_Pompey_the_Great%2C_Museo_Archeologico_Nazionale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pompey"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Galleria_Palatina%2C_Palazzo_Pitti%2C_Florence_%2826586289092%29.jpg/120px-Galleria_Palatina%2C_Palazzo_Pitti%2C_Florence_%2826586289092%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Galleria_Palatina%2C_Palazzo_Pitti%2C_Florence_%2826586289092%29.jpg/250px-Galleria_Palatina%2C_Palazzo_Pitti%2C_Florence_%2826586289092%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Galleria_Palatina%2C_Palazzo_Pitti%2C_Florence_%2826586289092%29.jpg/120px-Galleria_Palatina%2C_Palazzo_Pitti%2C_Florence_%2826586289092%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGalleria_Palatina%2C_Palazzo_Pitti%2C_Florence_(26586289092).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Chantilly_%2860%29%2C_mus%C3%A9e_Cond%C3%A9%2C_grande_galerie_de_peinture%2C_vue_g%C3%A9n%C3%A9rale_3.jpg/120px-Chantilly_%2860%29%2C_mus%C3%A9e_Cond%C3%A9%2C_grande_galerie_de_peinture%2C_vue_g%C3%A9n%C3%A9rale_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Chantilly_%2860%29%2C_mus%C3%A9e_Cond%C3%A9%2C_grande_galer